---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Finish Your Cut Edge with a Clean Neckband | Knit it Now";
const description =
  "Turn a raw cut edge into a clean, polished neckband with this guided machine knitting lesson.";
---

<Layout {title} {description} bodyClass="page--tight-header">
  <article class="help-hub-lesson" aria-labelledby="help-hub-lesson-title">
    <div class="help-hub-lesson__inner">
      <header class="help-hub-lesson__hero">
        <h1 id="help-hub-lesson-title" class="help-hub-lesson__title">
          Finish Your Cut Edge with a Clean Neckband
        </h1>
        <div class="help-hub-lesson__intro">
          <p>You’ve taken the brave step—you cut your knitting.</p>
          <p>
            Now let’s turn that raw edge into something clean, polished, and completely wearable.
          </p>
          <p>
            In this lesson, I’ll walk you through one of my favorite ways to finish a cut edge using
            a simple knitted neckband that looks beautiful on both sides.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div data-ms-content="members">
        <section class="help-hub-lesson__section" aria-label="Lesson video">
          <div class="help-hub-lesson__video-frame">
            <div class="help-hub-lesson__video-embed">
              <iframe
                src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1175910979"
                frameborder="0"
                allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture"
                allowfullscreen
              ></iframe>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="help-hub-lesson__section" aria-label="Guidance and reassurance">
          <div class="help-hub-lesson__prose">
            <p>
              This technique may feel like a lot the first time through—and that’s completely
              normal.
            </p>
            <p>
              That’s why working on a swatch first is so helpful. It gives you the chance to see how
              the stitches behave, how the band comes together, and how forgiving this process really
              is.
            </p>
            <p>
              You don’t need perfection here—you’re learning how the pieces fit together.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="help-hub-lesson__section" aria-labelledby="help-hub-lesson-steps-heading">
          <h2 id="help-hub-lesson-steps-heading" class="help-hub-lesson__section-heading">
            Step overview
          </h2>
          <ul class="help-hub-lesson__steps">
            <li>Measure or estimate stitches needed for your neckline</li>
            <li>Knit the first band piece with gentle tension shaping</li>
            <li>Rehang your garment with the cut edge facing you</li>
            <li>Knit the second band to mirror the first</li>
            <li>Join both band layers to encase the cut edge</li>
            <li>Bind off loosely for a clean finish</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="help-hub-lesson__section help-hub-lesson__section--close" aria-label="Closing encouragement">
          <div class="help-hub-lesson__prose">
            <p>Once you’ve done this once, everything starts to click.</p>
            <p>
              And the best part? You’re no longer limited by your stitch pattern—you can shape first,
              and finish beautifully after.
            </p>
            <p>Take your time, trust the process, and let your knitting guide you.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="help-hub-lesson__locked" data-ms-content="!members">
        <h2 class="help-hub-lesson__locked-heading">This lesson is for members</h2>
        <p class="help-hub-lesson__locked-text">
          Sign in with your member account to watch the video and follow along.
        </p>
        <div class="help-hub-lesson__locked-actions">
          <a href="#" data-ms-modal="login" class="help-hub-lesson__cta help-hub-lesson__cta--secondary">
            Log in
          </a>
          <a href="/membership" class="help-hub-lesson__cta">Become a member</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    .help-hub-lesson__inner {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 1rem 3.5rem;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__hero {
      padding-top: 0.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__title {
      font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.1rem);
      line-height: 1.25;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--kbm-green);
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__intro p {
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: #243015;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__intro p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__section {
      margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__section--close {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__section-heading {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--kbm-green);
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__prose p {
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: #243015;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__prose p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__video-frame {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto 2rem;
      border: 6px solid #ffffff;
      border-radius: 14px;
      overflow: hidden;
      background: #000;
      height: auto;
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__video-embed {
      position: relative;
      width: 100%;
      padding-top: 56.25%;
      height: 0;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__video-embed iframe {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      display: block;
      border: 0;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__steps {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: #243015;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__steps li {
      margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__steps li:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__locked {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      border-radius: 14px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(82, 104, 45, 0.22);
      background: rgba(82, 104, 45, 0.07);
      padding: clamp(1rem, 2.4vw, 1.6rem);
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__locked-heading {
      margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.3rem);
      color: #243015;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__locked-text {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      color: #3f4b35;
      line-height: 1.6;
      max-width: 62ch;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__locked-actions {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.65rem;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__cta {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0.72rem 1.05rem;
      border-radius: 10px;
      background: var(--kbm-green, #52682d);
      color: #fff;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1;
      transition: background 0.2s ease;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__cta:hover {
      background: var(--kbm-green-hover, #445626);
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__cta:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--kbm-green, #52682d);
      outline-offset: 2px;
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__cta--secondary {
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--kbm-green, #52682d);
      border: 2px solid var(--kbm-green, #52682d);
    }

    .help-hub-lesson__cta--secondary:hover {
      background: rgba(82, 104, 45, 0.08);
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
